---
title: "Stablecoin Blocklist Impact (Incident Response Blacklist)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_normal: sale/auction contract deployed with bidToken (e.g. USDC)
    q_normal --> q_investors_invest: investors invest bidToken into contract
    q_investors_invest --> q_blocklist_event: external token issuer blocklists contract address
    q_blocklist_event --> q_funds_locked: all bidToken transfers from contract revert
    q_funds_locked --> q_no_refund: refund() reverts (safeTransfer fails)
    q_funds_locked --> q_no_withdraw: withdrawRaisedCapital() reverts
    q_funds_locked --> q_no_cancel_return: cancel + withdrawIfCanceled reverts
    q_no_refund --> q_incident_response: Legion initiates incident response
    q_no_withdraw --> q_incident_response: Legion initiates incident response
    q_no_cancel_return --> q_incident_response: Legion initiates incident response
    q_incident_response --> [*]: emergencyWithdraw or external resolution required

    note right of q_blocklist_event
        INV-001: single contract blocklist affects ALL investors in that sale
        INV-002: blocklist is external to Legion protocol (token issuer action)
        INV-003: no on-chain mitigation exists within Legion contracts
    end note

    note right of q_funds_locked
        INV-004: emergencyWithdraw(receiver, token, amount) is only recovery path
        INV-005: emergencyWithdraw requires onlyLegion access
    end note
